// Package i3 is the i3bar protocol as a family: a status line is a tree of
// `block`s under a `bar`, and the running program writes it to stdout every
// time the state it reads changes.
//
// Nothing here is a platform. The family is generated by whichever host the
// build picks -- gtk4 or fyne -- because what it becomes is SNGL the host
// compiles: `block[go.language]` in `go.sngl` is a *language* override, and
// the protocol itself, in `protocol.sngl`, is written in SNGL.
